# Code owners for the files that control a Rust project's checks. Copy to
# .github/CODEOWNERS and replace @gaius-codius with the project's owner or team.
#
# On its own this file only requests reviews. It protects the checks when a branch
# ruleset on the default branch requires a pull request with "Require review from
# Code Owners": then no change that loosens a lint, a dependency policy, the
# toolchain or a workflow merges without the owner's approval, whoever (or whatever
# agent) wrote it. The Claude Code hook agent/claude-rust-protect-config.sh asks for
# the same files before an agent edits them; this is the gate that holds on the server.
#
# Later lines win, so keep project-specific entries below these.

# Lints and lint config. Cargo.toml also holds dependencies, so every manifest change
# needs the owner; narrow this if that's too much review.
Cargo.toml                  @gaius-codius
clippy.toml                 @gaius-codius
.clippy.toml                @gaius-codius

# Formatting, toolchain, test profiles, dependency policy, spelling.
rustfmt.toml                @gaius-codius
.rustfmt.toml               @gaius-codius
/rust-toolchain.toml        @gaius-codius
/rust-toolchain             @gaius-codius
/.config/nextest.toml       @gaius-codius
/deny.toml                  @gaius-codius
/typos.toml                 @gaius-codius
/_typos.toml                @gaius-codius
/.typos.toml                @gaius-codius

# CI, git hooks, secret scanning, and this file.
/.github/workflows/         @gaius-codius
/.github/actions/           @gaius-codius
/lefthook.yml               @gaius-codius
/.gitleaks.toml             @gaius-codius
/.github/CODEOWNERS         @gaius-codius
